# Experimental data. Far too large for git: the pva image stacks run to 110 MB
# each, over GitHub's hard 100 MB-per-file limit, and the directory holds
# ~558 MB in all. The viewers read these from disk; they are not part of the
# code and are not ours to publish.
*.h5
*.hdf
*.hdf5

# ...except one pair kept as a worked example: scan 152, a 101-frame psic_eta
# rocking curve. It exercises all three viewers, and because the angles move it
# gives the HKL map a real reciprocal-space volume rather than a single
# detector surface. 21.5 MB for the pair, so no git-lfs needed.
!tise2_2_00152_master.hdf
!pva_tise2_2_00152.h5

# Gridded reciprocal-space maps written by hkl_grid.py. Derived from the data
# above and regenerated on demand, tens of MB each.
*.vti

# Per-folder geometry corrections written by the HKL viewer. They belong to a
# beamtime and a diffractometer, not to the code.
hkl_setup.json

# Generated by plot_last_scan.py
last_scan.png

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Build metadata from `pip install -e .`
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Local tooling and machine-specific state
.claude/
logs/

# macOS
.DS_Store
